# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a strand whose per-strand instruction_budget_remaining reaches 0
#         yields back to the scheduler (soft yield) and is re-enqueued READY
#         rather than killed; it resumes on the next scheduler turn.
#
# blocked: per-strand soft-yield not observable via the public API — the
#          per-strand instruction budget is URBI_STRAND_BUDGET_MAX, a
#          compile-time macro (usched_cooperative.c) the runtime cannot
#          override; the chk-host-driver controls only the urbi_step budget,
#          not the per-strand budget, so it cannot force a mid-snippet soft
#          yield and resume.  Needs a runtime strand-budget knob.
#          v0.10.7-G residual.
# matrix-row: scheduler-budget
#
# Reason: observing soft-yield behaviour from a chk fixture requires the
# ## host: tunables header to override URBI_STRAND_BUDGET_MAX to a small value
# (e.g. 2 opcodes) so that a short urbiscript snippet triggers a budget
# exhaustion mid-run.  The chk runner does not support tunables headers until
# T39.  The soft-yield path itself is fully wired in dispatch_loop_until_yield
# (safepoint block; instruction_budget_remaining == 0 → sched_strand_yield).
#
# When T39 lands, implement this fixture by:
#   ## tunables: URBI_STRAND_BUDGET_MAX=2
#   ## host: step VM over multiple turns; assert strand resumes after yield
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 1
#   [00000002] 2
